A serious consideration should be made of moving Nethack to C++.

C++ will allow some more eligant code (WHO CARES!) and most
importantly allow a more GNERIC way of handling monsters.  My guess is
this move will make Nethack a smaler executable.  My experience with
porting C -> C++ is that my programs generally shrink 50% in source
size and 33% in executables.  

This means that NH3.0j won't be 789k! (on the PC) but 530k instead.
MUCH smaller and it might not need overlays.  (I doubt that)

I think it would also make more sense.  Why?  Think about it.  NH is
really Object oreinted.  If you use OOP language it will be MUCH
easier to implement.  

Perhaps it could be call NH4.0?  OR OOHack?

